# CogGuard Collaboration Rules

- Always respond in Simplified Chinese.
- If there are multiple reasonable implementation options, pause and present the options plus trade-offs before choosing one.
- If background, requirements, or data assumptions are missing, ask for clarification instead of guessing.
- Before substantial edits, briefly state the intended change and keep progress updates concise.
- Do not claim a feature is verified unless it was actually tested in the required environment.
- When discussing real crawlers, distinguish clearly between mock data, parsing/unit tests, and true end-to-end validation.
